WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.500
Efforts to ban flavored e-cigarettes,
while understandable, will cause more

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.660
harm than good.
Some vapers will simply resume smoking

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.880
deadly cigarettes; others will seek out
dangerous counterfeit vapes.

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.880
E-cigarettes are considerably safer than
cigarettes and flavors are a powerful

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.529
incentive for effective use by adults.
E-cigarettes deliver nicotine as an

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:30.700
aerosol, while cigarettes burn tobacco.
It's the smoke from burning tobacco,

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:35.600
not the nicotine, that contains carcinogenic tar.
Now, we don't know the health effects

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:40.170
of years of inhaling e-cigarette aerosol.
Researchers will need to follow vapers

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:45.720
for many years, and this uncertainty is
why non-smokers should not start to vape.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.920
One of the biggest concerns about teens —
that vaping leads to more teen smoking — has not

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:55.500
happened, so the FDA should not
ban flavors. Other steps can be taken to

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.000
reduce teen access to e-cigarettes.
Meanwhile, we need to protect safer

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.129
alternatives to cigarettes for those who
already vape, and the 35 million American

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:08.120
smokers who have yet to quit.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:11.820
What do you think? Should the US
ban flavored e-cigarettes?

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.509
Let us know in our poll.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:15.509 --> 00:01:20.040
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.049
more research and videos from AEI.

